# config/recipe.env -- WHAT is served. launch/up.sh reads it together with cluster.env (WHERE it runs).
#
# This is the configuration the published numbers were measured with (build "b072", 28 October 2026; see the README).
# The file is sourced by bash: M_VLLM_ARGS and M_DOCKER_EXTRA are built from short quoted pieces so that each group of
# settings can carry a comment. Every piece starts with a space; do not put anything else between the pieces.
#
# The placeholders in @...@ form (@MODEL_DIR@, @API_PORT@, @GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION@, @MASTER_ADDR@, @MASTER_PORT@,
# @ENGRAM_PACKED_DIR@) are filled from cluster.env before this file is read. Whatever is written here, the launcher
# forces the model path, --port, --master-addr, --master-port, --nnodes, --tensor-parallel-size and
# --gpu-memory-utilization to the cluster.env values, and adds --node-rank / --headless per rank.
#
# Every GB10 patch (patches/NNN-*.sh)
# is switched by one of the environment variables below and described in PATCHES.md. Set the same variables on all eight
# ranks: this file is the only place they are set, and the launcher gives it to every rank unchanged.
#
# Summary: tensor parallel 8 (experts split over all eight GPUs, stored at their native 288-column width), 1,048,576-token
# context, up to 128 sequences, 8,192-token prefill chunks, 43.5 GiB FP8 KV pool per node, DSpark speculative decoding (5 drafted
# tokens), Engram layers 1 and 14 read from node-local NVMe, FULL_DECODE_ONLY CUDA graphs whose private pool is shrunk by patch 043.

# ---- Image and patches ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The image built by image/build.sh (vLLM nightly e4a5b55 + the build-time GB10 edit).
M_IMAGE=dsv41-flash-sm121:n1

# Run patches/entrypoint.sh at container start: it applies patches/NNN-*.sh in order, then starts vLLM.
M_BOOT_ENTRYPOINT=recipe
M_PATCH_DIR=patches

# ---- vllm serve arguments -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model, API and parsers (thinking, tool calls). Text only: the vision encoder is not loaded.
M_VLLM_ARGS='@MODEL_DIR@ --served-model-name dsv41-flash-1017-uncen --host 0.0.0.0 --port @API_PORT@'
M_VLLM_ARGS+=' --tokenizer-mode deepseek_v41 --reasoning-parser deepseek_v41 --tool-call-parser deepseek_v41 --enable-auto-tool-choice'
M_VLLM_ARGS+=' --language-model-only'

# Context window, concurrency and prefill chunking. 128 sequences: the CUDA graphs below are captured up to 768 tokens
# (128 requests x 6 tokens). 8,192-token chunks, but only 4,096 tokens of a long prompt per step while other requests are active.
M_VLLM_ARGS+=' --max-model-len 1048576 --max-num-seqs 128 --max-num-batched-tokens 8192 --long-prefill-token-threshold 4096'
M_VLLM_ARGS+=' --enable-prefix-caching'

# Memory. The KV pool is pinned (43.5 GiB = 46707769344 bytes per node, 20,411,335 tokens); --gpu-memory-utilization is only the
# start-up free-memory check on GB10's unified memory. FP8 KV cache in DeepSeek's own format, 64-token blocks. The size is the
# largest that kept the head node at 8 GiB free or more in the worst-case order (a long prompt right after a busy period): it depends on
# the two memory patches below (043 and 045). Without them use 40 GiB (42949672960).
M_VLLM_ARGS+=' --gpu-memory-utilization @GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION@ --kv-cache-dtype fp8 --block-size 64 --kv-cache-memory-bytes 46707769344'

# Kernels: b12x fused MoE for the MXFP4 experts (native 288-column slice with patch 036), Marlin for the dense MXFP8 weights,
# FP8 indexer cache, indexer rows sharded over the ranks from 2,048 rows per chunk. vLLM's custom all-reduce is off (patch 012/018 take over).
M_VLLM_ARGS+=' --moe-backend b12x --linear-backend marlin --disable-custom-all-reduce'
M_VLLM_ARGS+=" --attention-config '{\"indexer_kv_dtype\":\"fp8\",\"indexer_tp_shard_min_rows\":2048}'"

# Engram n-gram tables: layers 1 and 14 are read from node-local NVMe (patches 016 and 030) instead of sitting in memory
# (23.6 GiB per node); 1 % of the rows read are verified against the checkpoint.
M_VLLM_ARGS+=" --engram-config '{\"cpu_offload\":false,\"nvme\":true,\"nvme_layers\":[1,14],\"nvme_verify_pct\":1}'"

# Parallelism: tensor parallel 8, one rank per node, vLLM's multiprocessing executor (the launcher sets the rank and the head node).
M_VLLM_ARGS+=' --tensor-parallel-size 8 --pipeline-parallel-size 1 --nnodes 8 --master-addr @MASTER_ADDR@ --master-port @MASTER_PORT@'
M_VLLM_ARGS+=' --distributed-executor-backend mp --load-format safetensors'

# DSpark speculative decoding: 5 drafted tokens per step from the draft blocks inside the checkpoint, probabilistic drafting,
# block verification, the drafter's top-2048 candidates (patch 013). Adaptive verification is not available on SM12x.
M_VLLM_ARGS+=" --speculative-config '{\"method\":\"dspark\",\"num_speculative_tokens\":5,\"draft_sample_method\":\"probabilistic\",\"rejection_sample_method\":\"block\",\"enable_adaptive_verification\":false,\"dspark_draft_topk\":2048}'"

# CUDA graphs for decode only, captured for every batch size the scheduler can produce (1 + 5 tokens per request, up to 128 requests).
M_VLLM_ARGS+=" --compilation-config '{\"cudagraph_mode\":\"FULL_DECODE_ONLY\",\"cudagraph_capture_sizes\":[5,6,10,12,15,18,20,24,25,30,35,36,40,42,45,48,50,54,55,60,65,66,70,72,75,78,80,84,85,90,95,96,100,102,105,108,110,114,115,120,125,126,130,132,135,138,140,144,145,150,155,156,160,162,165,168,170,174,175,180,185,186,190,192,195,198,200,204,205,210,215,216,220,222,225,228,230,234,235,240,245,246,250,252,255,258,260,264,265,270,275,276,280,282,285,288,290,294,295,300,305,306,310,312,315,318,320,324,325,330,335,336,340,342,345,348,350,354,355,360,365,366,370,372,375,378,380,384,385,390,395,396,400,402,405,408,410,414,415,420,425,426,430,432,435,438,440,444,445,450,455,456,460,462,465,468,470,474,475,480,485,486,490,492,495,498,500,504,505,510,515,516,520,522,525,528,530,534,535,540,545,546,550,552,555,558,560,564,565,570,575,576,580,582,585,588,590,594,595,600,605,606,610,612,615,618,620,624,625,630,635,636,640,642,648,654,660,666,672,678,684,690,696,702,708,714,720,726,732,738,744,750,756,762,768]}'"

# ---- Container environment (docker -e / -v) --------------------------------------------------------------------
# The launcher already sets the NCCL, RoCE and memory-lock options (see docker_run_cmd in launch/lib.sh); these are the recipe's.
# Each group names the patch it switches. A patch whose variable is absent is inert; the patch files stay installed.
M_DOCKER_EXTRA='-e NCCL_MAX_NCHANNELS=4 -e VLLM_ALLREDUCE_USE_FLASHINFER=0'

# Collectives for small messages (decode): patch 012 one-shot all-reduce over NCCL; patch 018 RoCE one-shot all-reduce / all-gather and the
# two-shot all-reduce up to 1 MiB, its CPU proxy thread on the last fast core.
M_DOCKER_EXTRA+=' -e VLLM_GB10_ONESHOT_AR=1 -e VLLM_GB10_ROCE=1 -e VLLM_GB10_ROCE_TWOSHOT_MAX_BYTES=1048576 -e GB10_TWOSHOT_PROXY_CPU=auto'

# Decode kernels: patch 025 mHC split configs for 6 and 12 tokens, patch 023 router GEMM through the CuTe dot-product kernel.
M_DOCKER_EXTRA+=' -e VLLM_GB10_MHC_SPLIT=6=4,8,128/12=6,8,128 -e VLLM_GB10_ROUTER_LL=1'

# DSpark drafter: patch 020 MXFP8 draft head and column-parallel main_proj, 024 the request's top-p on the draft distribution,
# 029 fused Markov bias, 038 top-k candidate gather (from 5 draft rows, first 4 calls double-checked against the stock path),
# 026 masked verification with the exact "chain" policy and 040 (its chain only where it is used).
M_DOCKER_EXTRA+=' -e VLLM_DSPARK_FP8_HEAD=1 -e VLLM_DSPARK_MAIN_PROJ_TP=1 -e VLLM_DSPARK_DRAFT_TOP_P=1 -e VLLM_DSPARK_MARKOV_FUSED=1'
M_DOCKER_EXTRA+=' -e VLLM_DSPARK_TOPK_GATHER=1 -e VLLM_DSPARK_TOPK_GATHER_MIN_ROWS=5 -e VLLM_DSPARK_TOPK_GATHER_CHECK=4'
M_DOCKER_EXTRA+=' -e VLLM_GB10_MV=chain -e VLLM_GB10_MV_SKIP_INELIGIBLE=1'

# Prefill: patch 021 MXFP8 W8A8 GEMMs from 512 rows, patch 022 sequence-parallel mHC (layers 0-19) with the Engram all-to-all,
# patch 028 two-half communication/compute overlap on top of it. The control file is an optional runtime switch on the head node
# (HF_CACHE_DIR/dsv41-p028.ctl containing "off" or "on"; absent means on). The self-test runs at the first long prefill and only
# reports numeric differences; CRITERION=noise measures the run-to-run noise floor first. INDEXER=comm2 gives the indexer's top-k exchange its own NCCL communicator.
M_DOCKER_EXTRA+=' -e VLLM_MXFP8_PREFILL_W8A8=1 -e VLLM_GB10_PREFILL_SP=1 -e VLLM_GB10_PREFILL_SP_ENGRAM=a2a'
M_DOCKER_EXTRA+=' -e VLLM_GB10_PREFILL_SP_OVERLAP=1 -e VLLM_GB10_PREFILL_SP_OVERLAP_CTL=/cache/huggingface/dsv41-p028.ctl'
M_DOCKER_EXTRA+=' -e VLLM_GB10_PREFILL_SP_OVERLAP_LOG_EVERY=10 -e VLLM_GB10_PREFILL_SP_OVERLAP_SELFTEST=report'
M_DOCKER_EXTRA+=' -e VLLM_GB10_PREFILL_SP_OVERLAP_CRITERION=noise -e VLLM_GB10_PREFILL_SP_OVERLAP_INDEXER=comm2'

# b12x MoE kernels: patch 036 stores and reads the 288-column expert slice natively (no padding), patch 037 uses 64-row tiles for
# prefill-size launches from 16 routed rows per expert.
M_DOCKER_EXTRA+=' -e B12X_COMPACT_N32=1 -e B12X_COMPACT_PREFILL_TILE_M=64 -e B12X_COMPACT_PREFILL_MIN_ROWS_PER_EXPERT=16'

# Engram rows from NVMe: packed rows (one 512-byte read per row) built by tools/engram_pack.py, required (no silent fallback),
# the 1 % verification re-reads run after the GPU has its rows. The directory is mounted read-only at the same path.
M_DOCKER_EXTRA+=' -e ENGRAM_NVME_PACKED_DIR=@ENGRAM_PACKED_DIR@ -e ENGRAM_NVME_PACKED=require -e ENGRAM_NVME_VERIFY_AFTER=1'
M_DOCKER_EXTRA+=' -v @ENGRAM_PACKED_DIR@:@ENGRAM_PACKED_DIR@:ro'

# Memory (patches 043 and 045): the decode sparse indexer's rows run in chunks of at most 512 MiB of temporaries inside the CUDA
# graphs and the drafter's graphs share the main graphs' capture stream (043: the graphs' private pool shrinks from 3.8 to 0.68 GiB
# per rank); the token embedding is vocab-parallel again (045 switches patch 015's replicated table off: 1.07 GiB per rank back).
# Leave EMBED_TP out to keep 015's replicated embedding, and lower the KV pool by 1 GiB.
M_DOCKER_EXTRA+=' -e VLLM_GB10_EMBED_TP=1 -e VLLM_GB10_INDEXER_DECODE_CHUNK_MB=512 -e VLLM_GB10_SHARED_CAPTURE_STREAM=1'

# Diagnostics only (patch 032): the CUDA caching allocator's statistics of every worker, one log line a minute. Patch 042 adds an
# on-demand snapshot (touch HF_CACHE_DIR/dsv41-memsnap.trigger on a node) and needs nothing here.
M_DOCKER_EXTRA+=' -e VLLM_GB10_MEMSTATS=60'

# General: model-execution timeout, kernel and compile caches under the cache directory of cluster.env, CuTe architecture, no CUDA-graph
# memory estimate (it is wrong on unified memory), allocator mode, NCCL log to stderr. (The image already switches off vLLM's
# usage reporting: VLLM_NO_USAGE_STATS=1 and DO_NOT_TRACK=1 are set in image/Dockerfile.)
M_DOCKER_EXTRA+=' -e VLLM_EXECUTE_MODEL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=600 -e CUTE_DSL_ARCH=sm_121a -e VLLM_MEMORY_PROFILER_ESTIMATE_CUDAGRAPHS=0'
M_DOCKER_EXTRA+=' -e TILELANG_CACHE_DIR=/cache/huggingface/tilelang-cache -e FLASHINFER_WORKSPACE_BASE=/cache/huggingface/flashinfer-base'
M_DOCKER_EXTRA+=' -e VLLM_CACHE_ROOT=/cache/huggingface/vllm-cache -e TRITON_CACHE_DIR=/cache/huggingface/triton-cache'
M_DOCKER_EXTRA+=' -e NCCL_DEBUG_FILE=/dev/stderr -e PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True'
